          Severity: HIGH                                                                                      
          Affected versions of vllm are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling.   
          vLLM is vulnerable to an unauthorized internal state disclosure and potential denial-of-service in  
          multi-node tensor parallel deployments. The primary host binds an XPUB ZeroMQ socket on all         
          interfaces, allowing any network client with access to receive internal state metadata and flood the
          broadcaster with unread connections, possibly degrading or blocking communication between vLLM      
          hosts.                                                                                              
                                                                                                              
