    ❯❱ prismjs - CVE-2024-53382
          Severity: MODERATE                                                                                 
          Affected versions of prismjs are vulnerable to Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code       
          Injection') / Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting').
          PrismJS before 1.30.0 contains a DOM Clobbering vulnerability: the library's core initialization   
          reads document.currentScript without verifying it is a <script> element, so an attacker-injected   
          HTML element (e.g. <img name="currentScript">) can shadow document.currentScript. Combined with the
          autoloader plugin, this lets an attacker control the base path used to load language components,   
          resulting in loading scripts from an attacker-controlled origin and cross-site scripting. Because  
          the vulnerable code runs at library load time, every importer of an affected version is exposed;   
          upgrade to 1.30.0 or later.                                                                        
                                                                                                             
