   ❯❯❱ serialize-javascript - GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq
          Severity: HIGH                                                                                      
          Affected versions of serialize-javascript are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of Directives in
          Statically Saved Code ('Static Code Injection'). `serialize-javascript` is vulnerable to code       
          injection when serializing non-plain objects that masquerade as `RegExp` or `Date`. The library     
          sanitizes `RegExp.source` but interpolates `RegExp.flags` (and similarly the result of              
          `Date.prototype.toISOString()`) directly into the generated JavaScript without escaping, allowing an
          attacker who controls the input to `serialize()` to inject arbitrary JavaScript into the serialized 
          output. If the consumer later evaluates that string (e.g., via `eval`, `new Function`, or embedding 
          in a `<script>` tag), the injected payload executes and can lead to remote code execution in        
          Node.js.                                                                                            
                                                                                                              
